/* book exam traps: Placing the anti-aliasing filter after the sampler. It is then a digital filter, and the alias is already inside the samples. | Thinking a faster sampler can remove an alias that is already in recorded samples; the mixing has already happened. | Reading the alias of 1300 Hz at fs = 1000 Hz as 1300 − 500. Fold about multiples of fs, not about fs/2: |1300 − 1000| = 300 Hz. | Saying every alias keeps its amplitude. That holds for one isolated cosine; components folding onto the same frequency add or cancel. | Mixing up the guard band (fs − 2fmax) with the strict transition band (fs/2 − fmax), which is half of it. */
